// Talks to Vercel's "Prisma Postgres" storage integration, which is fronted
// entirely by Prisma's Accelerate proxy (db.prisma.io) — there is no plain
// postgres:// endpoint exposed for this resource, only this prisma+postgres://
// one. That's why the client needs the Accelerate extension (see api/_db.js).
//
// No models are declared here on purpose: api/migrate.js and api/_db.js use
// raw SQL ($executeRawUnsafe/$queryRawUnsafe) instead of Prisma's typed query
// API, so this schema only exists to point the generated client at the right
// database.
// The newer "prisma-client" generator emits ESM/TypeScript output, which doesn't
// fit this project's plain CommonJS serverless functions (no build step). This
// classic generator still produces a require()-able CJS client in Prisma 7.
generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

// Prisma 7 removed `url` from the datasource block entirely — the connection
// string is passed to the PrismaClient constructor in code instead (see
// api/_db.js). This block only declares the provider.
datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}
